# Absenta API Development Patterns

## Authentication & Authorization
```javascript
// Always use these middleware for protected routes
app.get('/api/admin/endpoint', authenticateToken, requireRole(['admin']), async (req, res) => {
    // Endpoint logic
});
```

## Response Patterns
```javascript
// Success responses
res.success(data, 'Operation successful');

// Error responses
res.error('Error message', 'Operation failed');
res.unauthorized('Invalid credentials');
res.notFound('Resource not found');
```

## Database Query Patterns (Based on absenta13.sql)
```javascript
// User queries - use users table (not pengguna)
const [rows] = await db.execute(
    'SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = ? AND role = ?',
    [username, role]
);

// Subject queries - use mapel table with id_mapel
const [subjects] = await db.execute(
    'SELECT * FROM mapel WHERE status = "aktif" ORDER BY nama_mapel'
);

// JOIN patterns with users table
const [data] = await db.execute(`
    SELECT g.*, u.username, u.status as user_status
    FROM guru g
    LEFT JOIN users u ON g.user_id = u.id
`);

// Schedule queries with multi-teacher support
const [schedules] = await db.execute(`
    SELECT 
        j.*,
        m.nama_mapel,
        k.nama_kelas,
        g.nama as nama_guru,
        'primary' as role
    FROM jadwal j
    JOIN mapel m ON j.mapel_id = m.id_mapel
    JOIN kelas k ON j.kelas_id = k.id_kelas
    JOIN guru g ON j.guru_id = g.id_guru
    WHERE j.status = 'aktif'
    
    UNION ALL
    
    SELECT 
        j.*,
        m.nama_mapel,
        k.nama_kelas,
        g.nama as nama_guru,
        jgt.role
    FROM jadwal j
    JOIN mapel m ON j.mapel_id = m.id_mapel
    JOIN kelas k ON j.kelas_id = k.id_kelas
    JOIN jadwal_guru_tambahan jgt ON j.id_jadwal = jgt.jadwal_id
    JOIN guru g ON jgt.guru_id = g.id_guru
    WHERE j.status = 'aktif' AND jgt.status = 'aktif'
`);
```

## Error Handling
```javascript
try {
    // Database operations
    const [result] = await db.execute(query, params);
    console.log('✅ Operation successful');
    res.success(result, 'Operation completed');
} catch (error) {
    console.error('❌ Operation failed:', error);
    res.error('Internal server error', 'Operation failed');
}
```

## Validation Patterns
```javascript
// Required field validation
if (!username || !password) {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Username and password are required' });
}

// Uniqueness validation
const [existing] = await db.execute('SELECT id FROM pengguna WHERE nama_pengguna = ?', [username]);
if (existing.length > 0) {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Username already exists' });
}
```

## Caching Patterns
```javascript
// Use cache middleware for GET endpoints
app.get('/api/endpoint', 
    cacheMiddleware(300, (req) => `cache:key:${JSON.stringify(req.query)}`), 
    async (req, res) => {
        // Endpoint logic
    }
);
```